# Docker only reads a .dockerignore from the root of the build context. This
# Dockerfile builds with context=packages/gp-ai (see its header comment), so
# the file that actually governs this build is packages/gp-ai/.dockerignore
# one level up — its **/tests/, __pycache__/, and .venv/ patterns are
# recursive and already exclude the equivalent paths under autopilot/. Its
# bare *.md / !README.md pair is NOT recursive (an unprefixed *.md only
# matches at the context root), so nested files like autopilot/README.md and
# autopilot/agent/stages/*.md pass through either way — which is what you
# want, since main.py reads the stage *.md files at container run time. This
# file is a safety net for the same tests/__pycache__/.venv excludes if this
# Dockerfile is ever built with context=packages/gp-ai/autopilot directly
# instead.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
*.md
!README.md
**/tests/
**/test_*.py
**/*_test.py
